# Python API to MATLAB client verification

## Goal

Maintain MATLAB API clients (`+api/+clients/`) as faithful mirrors of Python sync HTTP clients (`soc/common/clients/` in Ultrasat.git nova). Verify via headless debug scripts (`+debug/+ultrasat/+api/+clients/`).

## Source of truth

**Python is canonical.** Never invent or rename fields in MATLAB.

| Layer | Python path |
|-------|-------------|
| Sync client | `Ultrasat.git/python/prj/nova/soc/common/clients/` |
| API models | `soc/common/models/.../api/` |
| Domain models | `soc/common/models/.../domain/` |
| FastAPI service | `soc/platform/<name>/api.py` or mission paths |

| Layer | MATLAB path |
|-------|-------------|
| Clients | `+api/+clients/` |
| Debug | `+debug/+ultrasat/+api/+clients/` |
| HTTP base | `ClientBase.m`, `ClientFactory.m` |

## Environment

| Variable | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `SOC_PATH` | Must contain `config/services.json` and `log/` |
| `SOC_API_KEY` | Sent in `api-key` header by `ClientBase.postRequest` |

`services.json` `mode`: `direct` (per-service ports) or `nginx` (`base_api_url + service_path`).

## MATLAB launcher

```powershell
& "C:\Matlab\R2025b\bin\matlab.exe" -batch "<statement>" 2>&1 | Tee-Object -FilePath "<run.log>"
```

Sanity check:

```powershell
& "C:\Matlab\R2025b\bin\matlab.exe" -batch "debug.ultrasat.api.clients.debug_ClientFactory" 2>&1
```

## Iteration loop

1. Read Python client + response model first
2. Confirm MATLAB client sends/reads only those fields
3. Run matching `debug_*` with `-batch`
4. Fix MATLAB until struct matches Python contract

## Forbidden

- No guessing API field names or types
- No GUI changes from this loop
- No `error()` from client methods — return `struct('status','error','message',...)`
- Do not add MATLAB methods without a MATLAB caller
- Never touch `+clients/obsolete/` or `+debug/+ultrasat/+api/+clients/obsolete/`

## Common pitfalls

- Constructor argument lists must match the body (no undefined `ApiKey` in constructor if not declared)
- `-batch` requires AstroPack path via `startup.m`
- `jsondecode` may collapse single-element arrays to scalar struct
- Datetimes: `JsonUtils.json2struct` uses `DateTimeUtils.convertStringToDatetime`
